From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:01:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 051/160] hjviewer: ui: peer-tabs: pill tabs, one search field,
 calm empty states

The bar above the peer list and the panes under it in the app's look
(common/hjv_style.dart), on the desktop and the phone:

- Tabs: icon pills, the selected one primary on primarySoft instead of the
  black underline, the others textSecondary with the hover colour; 20 px
  icons, tooltips kept. On the phone a tab and a button keep upstream's
  40 px and 28 px, which _portraitRightActions plans the bar with.
- Bar buttons (search, refresh, select, view, sort, tags, More, the
  multi-select bar): 20 px icons in textSecondary on a rounded hover, the
  tags toggle primary on primarySoft while the panel shows, delete in danger.
- Search: one field of the bar's height with the icon, the text and the
  close button inside and the primary ring while focused (the theme's ring
  used to sit on the inner field).
- View and sort menus: the heading as a small section title.
- Empty lists: the tab's icon on a soft tile, the tip's first line as the
  title and the rest below; a tab that needs a login shows its icon and
  name above a 40 px login button.
- Address book and accessible devices panes: side panels as cards, the
  book name left-aligned, tags as rounded chips that end in an ellipsis
  inside the panel, the device list as rounded rows with a soft avatar and
  the selected row primary on primarySoft.
- Desktop status bar: 36 px, 13 px textSecondary, the dot in the palette's
  status colours, aligned with the content's 12 px edge.

Upstream's builders stay unused next to the new _hjv ones. Texts,
translate() keys, callbacks and widget keys are unchanged.

After an independent review (screens in light and dark, the diff, the code rules):

- Side panels: each accessible-devices row gets its own Material and the
  address book's selector one above the card's fill, so their hover and the
  phone's ripple show again; per row, so the ink stays clipped when the list
  scrolls. The devices panel is 200 px like the address book's, so Korean
  names fit.
- Banners: on the desktop the network and error banners end 12 px before
  the edge, where the bar above them ends.
- Search: the close button hovers in hoverStrong on its own Material instead
  of the border workaround. Below 720 px of window the tabs take upstream's
  40 px pitch and the open field upstream's 140 px, so the tabs stay on
  screen with the search open.
- Phone More menu: the card colour with a border like the other menus. Tab
  drag: a transparent proxy, so the dragged tab stays a pill.
- A search or a filter that matches nothing shows the empty placeholder.
- The HJViewer comments are one line each.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
